SKETCH banners as normative**: [BP-CAN-DATA] §1.5.2, [BP-CAN-ENUM] §1.5.4, [BP-TRANSPORT-I2C] §6.5,
the `ttl` / `cid` rows of [BP-MSG-OPT-FIELDS], and the Retain column of [BP-MQTT-QOS] describe a
target, not the wire. Two known open defects are recorded against the reference implementation and
are the CODE's to fix, not this document's: first-match scope auto-resolution ([BP-NS-AUTO-RESOLVE]
/ [BP-C3]) and unimplemented MQTT retain ([BP-MQTT-QOS]).
